target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestTheDecodeErrorNamesWhatTheOperatorMustGoFix'
expect: the cap must say how many gates it elided
why:    2,000 bad gates on one row produced a 14 KB message. The cap has to ELIDE and say so: silently printing the first eight would hide the scale, which is the same failure as printing all of them in the other direction.
--- old
	if len(bad) > maxNamedGates {
		extra, bad = len(bad)-maxNamedGates, bad[:maxNamedGates]
	}
--- new
	_ = maxNamedGates
